Z||000000||DreXteR||09-26-2001||11:37 PM||||Maybe this is not too techie but I need to know. Well Im looking forward to buy a shift knob, the guy told me that is universal and will fit. Is the fiero shifter dif, thicker, larger or so??<BR>I will not buy somthing that not fit.<P>Thanx<P>DreX||||reg||5
Z||000001||Formula88||09-26-2001||11:40 PM||||Well, the Fiero shift knob is threaded for a 16mm shaft with 1.5mm pitch threads.  Universal knobs just fit over the shaft and have set screws to hold them in place, so the only thing you need to make sure of it will it fit over a 16mm shaft? ||||reg||6
Z||000002||DreXteR||09-26-2001||11:55 PM||||Thanx for the fast reply Formula88.,   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>DreX||||reg||10
Z||000003||Alex4mula||09-27-2001||09:18 AM||||DreXteR; At least in my Formula no universal shift knob worked. It was too small (inner diameter). That included the MOMO ones too. But is not hard to make it fit. I was in love with this MOMO carbon fiber model that I just bought it. What I did was to take some coarse sand paper (80-120) and slowly reduced the diameter of the shift knob enough for the MOMO to get in. Took me about half hour. Actually I think I have a normal heigh shifter which I did that (piror to replace with short unit). Not sure. Just have a vacuum cleaner while you do it to suck the dust. The original Fiero knob will still fit too after it.<BR>||||reg||1
